Recommends: homelab-api, homelab-dovecot, homelab-postfix, homelab-audit
Description: Internal IMAP/SMTP relay behind homelab-api's mail gateway
 A Mojolicious app with no public address and, for anything mail-
 related, no database: it exists purely so homelab-api's
 /api/v1/mail/* gateway routes have something to forward to that
 actually speaks IMAP/SMTP, so a client (homelab-cli or any
 third-party script) never needs to know dovecot's or postfix's
 address -- only homelab-api's. Every request is authenticated the same
 way as every other homelab-* service (the caller's homelab-api JWT,
 re-verified here via introspect), and that same JWT is handed to
 dovecot/postfix as the XOAUTH2 bearer token -- the identical mechanism
 homelab-roundcube's SSO login already uses. Registers itself in the
 service registry with an internal host/port only; never fronted by
 homelab-webproxy. Holds one narrow Postgres grant (INSERT on
 audit.queue) purely for the mail-send audit trail -- see
 homelab-audit's own README.md.
